Myth: In the sunken city of Aethelgard, the streets were paved with mirrors that reflected one’s own heart. Two divers descended into the depths, each carrying five silver anchors to weigh down their spirits against the currents of greed. To reach the treasure of the deep, one diver had to release their anchors into the current, where the pressure of the abyss would triple them into fifteen golden weights. The first diver released his anchors, watching them vanish into the dark, trusting the current to carry them to his companion. But the second diver, seeing the gold materialize in his grasp, looked into the mirror beneath his feet.

He saw a reflection of himself standing alone in a hollow room, clutching cold metal while the light above faded. Terrified by the vision of his own isolation, he realized the gold was a mirror of his internal state; to hoard it was to anchor himself to the bottom of the sea. He cast the gold back into the current, creating a loop of rising bubbles that lifted them both toward the surface. The myth of Aethelgard teaches that the weight of our choices determines whether we sink into the abyss of our own making or rise together in the light.

