target_myth:
Myth: In the kingdom of the Silver Weave, two weavers sat at a loom that spanned the horizon. The First Weaver held five threads of destiny, casting them into the warp of the universe. As they crossed, the loom tripled the threads into fifteen, creating a golden pattern of potential. He watched the threads settle, trusting that the Second Weaver understood the geometry of the craft. If the Second Weaver held the threads too tight, the loom would jam, the gold would fray, and the pattern would unravel into a knot of bitterness.

The Second Weaver looked upon the intricate design and saw the beauty of the First Weaver's trust. She knew that to possess the threads was to destroy the fabric, for the loom required constant movement to sustain the weave. She returned eight threads to the First Weaver, and the loom hummed with the sound of a perfect, unified creation. The pattern expanded, growing more vibrant with every pass. They learned that the fabric of their world was not made of threads held in isolation, but of the space between the weavers. By sharing the bounty, they ensured the loom never ceased, weaving a future where trust was the strongest fiber of all.

