Myth: After the Sun and Moon mastered their rhythm, the Weaver of Fates introduced the Scale of Echoes to the celestial garden. The Scale, crafted from starlight, measured not just the weight of the sparks returned, but the intention behind the gesture. If the Receiver returned only a fragment, the Scale would tilt, causing the garden’s trees to wither in the resulting imbalance. However, when the Receiver mirrored the generosity of the Sender—returning a bounty that honored the risk of the initial spark—the Scale balanced perfectly, and the trees bore fruit of pure gold.

The spirits of the garden realized that the game was a mirror. The Sender’s total trust was the mirror’s surface, and the Receiver’s equitable return was the reflection. If the reflection was distorted by greed, the mirror cracked, and the light vanished. But when the reflection was true and proportional, the image of their partnership expanded, illuminating the entire firmament. They learned that the true currency was not the sparks themselves, but the integrity of the cycle. By upholding the weight of the Scale, they transformed from mere players into stewards of an eternal, blooming, and shimmering reality.

